  {
   "id": 548305,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "For many viruses to penetrate the cell membrane and complete their replication inside the cell, the virus must attach to their host cells. Describe how a virus attaches to a host cell.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1077011,
     "content_html": "A virus uses its cellular structure to attach to a host cell."
    },
    {
     "id": 1077012,
     "content_html": "A virus uses a plasma membrane to connect to a host cell."
    },
    {
     "id": 1077013,
     "content_html": "A virus uses matrix proteins to attach to a host cell."
    },
    {
     "id": 1077014,
     "content_html": "Viruses use viral receptors to attach to a host cell."
    }
   ],
